# M6.3 acceptance: Project > Instructions... edits the open project's
# CLAUDE.md. Run it with tests/acceptance/m6.3.sh, which builds the fixture in
# /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.3, a scratch HOME and the logging fake sidecar of
# M6.2, and checks the files and the sidecar log after the run. The run is
#   scripts/shot.sh -o <out> -s tests/acceptance/m6.3.steps -- \
#     env HOME=/tmp/agentic-reader-m6.3/home \
#       READER_SIDECAR_CMD=<worktree>/tests/acceptance/m6.2-fake-sidecar.sh \
#       READER_FAKE_LOG=/tmp/agentic-reader-m6.3/fake.log \
#       ./build/app/agentic-reader
# No file on the command line, and an empty HOME, so no project is open at
# start.
#
# Fixture (F = /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.3):
#   F/proj/.reader/        empty: proj is a saved project
#   F/proj/paper.pdf       tests/data/sample.pdf (3 pages, "Page One")
#   F/proj/CLAUDE.md       4 lines, ending with a newline:
#                            # Notes du projet
#                            Citez les numéros de page — toujours.
#                            iiiiiiiiii|
#                            MMMMMMMMMM|
#   F/loose/single.pdf     sample.pdf; no CLAUDE.md, no .reader/ (unsaved)
#   F/expect/proj-original.md   copy of the original proj/CLAUDE.md
#   F/expect/proj-saved.md      the original plus "Always answer in French.\n"
#   F/expect/loose-saved.md     "Answer briefly." with no newline
#
# Interface choices where the spec is silent (the implementer conforms or
# files a TEST DISPUTE):
#   - The menu bar is File, Edit, Project, Help. The new "&Project" menu
#     (Alt+P) holds "&Instructions..." (I picks it in the open menu).
#   - With no project open the item is disabled: there is no folder to put
#     CLAUDE.md in. It is enabled for a saved project and also for an
#     unsaved one (M6.2): CLAUDE.md lives in the project folder, not in
#     .reader/, so editing it does not save the project. The sidecar already
#     runs an unsaved project's chats in that folder.
#   - The dialog (InstructionsDialog) is modal. Its title contains
#     "Instructions". It holds a multiline wxTextCtrl in a monospace font
#     (wxFONTFAMILY_TELETYPE) with the content of <root>/CLAUDE.md, or empty
#     when the file is missing, and two buttons: wxID_SAVE labelled "&Save"
#     (Alt+S presses it) and wxID_CANCEL (Escape presses it). The text
#     control has the focus when the dialog opens, so Ctrl+End and typing
#     edit the text.
#   - Save writes the control's text to <root>/CLAUDE.md byte for byte (no
#     newline added or removed) through saveInstructions() in
#     app/src/project/Instructions.h (tests/test_instructions.cpp), closes
#     the dialog, and then shows the note in a message box: the instructions
#     apply to new chats, and chats already open keep the instructions they
#     started with. Return closes the message box. A failed save shows an
#     error and keeps the dialog open with the text (not driven here).
#   - Cancel (or Escape) closes the dialog without writing and without a
#     note or a confirmation, even after an edit.
#   - The sidecar is told nothing: new chats start the CLI in the project
#     folder with setting_sources=["project"], so each reads CLAUDE.md
#     itself (sidecar/reader_sidecar/chats.py, sidecar/tests/test_chats.py).
#     No new_chat or open_project is sent because of a save.
#   - The project tree lists PDFs only (M6.2), so CLAUDE.md never appears in
#     it.
#
# Geometry at 1400x900 (see m6.2.steps): menu bar y 0..27, toolbar y 28..68,
# left pane x 0..220, PDF pane x 225..980, status bar y 876..900.
wait 3

key alt+p
wait 1

# No project is open (empty HOME, no file given). The Project menu is open
# under "Project" in the menu bar, between Edit and Help, and shows
# "Instructions..." greyed out (disabled).
shot no-project-menu

key i
wait 2

# Pressing I on the disabled item opened nothing: no Instructions dialog and
# no message box. The Project menu may still be open; nothing else changed.
shot no-project-no-dialog

key Escape
wait 1
key ctrl+o
wait 2
key alt+Home
wait 1
key ctrl+l
wait 1
key space
key Home
run xdotool type --delay 0 /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.3/proj/paper.pdf
key End BackSpace
wait 1
key Return
wait 3

# paper.pdf is open in the saved project proj: the header names "proj" (no
# "Unsaved project"), the tree shows only paper.pdf, the PDF pane shows
# "Page One", status field 0 "paper.pdf".
shot proj-open

key alt+p
wait 1

# The Project menu is open and "Instructions..." is enabled (normal text,
# not greyed out).
shot project-menu

key i
wait 2

# The Instructions dialog is open over the main window, its title contains
# "Instructions", with Save and Cancel buttons. Its text area shows the four
# lines of proj/CLAUDE.md and nothing else: "# Notes du projet", "Citez les
# numéros de page — toujours." (é and the long dash drawn correctly, not as
# boxes or "Ã©"), "iiiiiiiiii|" and "MMMMMMMMMM|". The font is monospace:
# the two '|' are in the same column. No "Claude Code" anywhere.
shot dialog-loaded

key ctrl+End
type DISCARD ME
wait 1

# The text area now has a fifth line "DISCARD ME" below "MMMMMMMMMM|". The
# first four lines are unchanged.
shot dialog-edit-to-cancel

key Escape
wait 2
run cmp /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.3/proj/CLAUDE.md /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.3/expect/proj-original.md

# Escape (Cancel) closed the dialog without asking anything and without the
# "new chats" note: only the main window is visible, as in proj-open.
# CLAUDE.md is unchanged (checked by the run step).
shot cancelled

key alt+p
wait 1
key i
wait 2

# The dialog reopened from the file: the same four lines as in
# dialog-loaded, and no "DISCARD ME".
shot reopened-after-cancel

key ctrl+End
type Always answer in French.
key Return
wait 1

# The text area shows the four original lines and a fifth line "Always
# answer in French." The caret is on the empty line below it.
shot dialog-edit-to-save

key alt+s
wait 2
run cmp /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.3/proj/CLAUDE.md /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.3/expect/proj-saved.md

# Save wrote CLAUDE.md (checked by the run step: the original four lines,
# UTF-8 intact, plus "Always answer in French." and a newline). The dialog
# is closed and a message box shows the note: the instructions apply to new
# chats, and chats already open keep the instructions they started with.
# No "Claude Code" in it.
shot saved-note

key Return
wait 1
key alt+p
wait 1
key i
wait 2

# The message box is gone. The reopened dialog shows the saved text: the
# four original lines and "Always answer in French.", in the monospace font.
shot reopened-after-save

key Escape
wait 1
run cmp /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.3/proj/CLAUDE.md /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.3/expect/proj-saved.md
key ctrl+o
wait 2
key alt+Home
wait 1
key ctrl+l
wait 1
key space
key Home
run xdotool type --delay 0 /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.3/loose/single.pdf
key End BackSpace
wait 1
key Return
wait 3
run test ! -e /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.3/loose/.reader
key alt+p
wait 1

# single.pdf is open in the unsaved project loose: the header says "Unsaved
# project" with a "Save as project" button, the tree shows only single.pdf,
# status field 0 "single.pdf". The Project menu is open and
# "Instructions..." is enabled.
shot unsaved-project-menu

key i
wait 2

# The Instructions dialog is open and its text area is empty (loose has no
# CLAUDE.md), with the monospace text area, Save and Cancel as before.
shot unsaved-dialog-empty

type Answer briefly.
wait 1
key alt+s
wait 2
run cmp /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.3/loose/CLAUDE.md /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.3/expect/loose-saved.md
run test ! -e /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.3/loose/.reader

# Save created loose/CLAUDE.md holding exactly "Answer briefly." (no newline
# added) and did not save the project: no loose/.reader/ (both checked by
# the run steps). The dialog is closed and the "new chats" note is shown as
# in saved-note. Behind it the header still says "Unsaved project".
shot unsaved-saved-note

key Return
wait 1

# The note is closed. The main window shows loose as an unsaved project
# ("Unsaved project" and the "Save as project" button), the tree still
# shows only single.pdf (CLAUDE.md is not a PDF), single.pdf is open.
shot unsaved-after-note
